sweep_cost.py: full-sweep cost from the stress run's measured rates
   rates  : stress-final-item-rates.txt (derived by stress_records.py from the final metrics.jsonl)
   report : stress-final-report.txt      cross-checks: the lead's stress-item-rates.txt, stress-report-0655.txt
   year   : 31557600 s (Julian); month = year / 12; one weekend of the card = 219550 s (the final report's 'on the card')

CHECK the final report states the run's seconds on the card                        ok (219550 s)
CHECK the final derived file has the nine columns this script reads                ok (9 columns)
CHECK the rates file has 182 data rows (183 lines with its header)                 ok (182)
CHECK 68 distinct items in the rates file (14 exhaustive + 54 random)              ok (68)
CHECK every item belongs to a family with a stated unit and space                  ok []
CHECK the final report lists 54 random and 14 exhaustive items                     ok (54 random, 14 exhaustive)
CHECK every item has a quad row (the lead's per-tile convention)                   ok []
CHECK all 68 items' slices and cases equal the final report's tables exactly, summed over images ok []
CHECK the lead's earlier rates file has the nine columns this script reads         ok (9 columns)
CHECK the lead's earlier rates file is never ahead of the final record on any item ok []
CHECK the 06:55 report is never ahead of the final record on any item              ok []
CHECK the lead's medians (07:17, rows with >= 5 slices) agree with the final derivation within 3% ok (178 medians compared; the widest 0.59% at ('cvtto64-rmm', 'quad'))
CHECK the exhaustive items' count column is 0 everywhere (so cases/s is their rate) ok 
CHECK the random items' count rates are all positive                               ok 
CHECK scaleb32: cases_sum is within 0.1% of count_sum (count IS checks, not operands) ok (11722895360 vs 11719933952)
CHECK cvtfrom32: cases_sum is 4 x count_sum (4 source types a lane)                ok (50470060032 vs 12617515008)
CHECK cvtto32: cases_sum is between 1 x and 4 x count_sum (in-range pairs only)    ok (ratio 2.27)
CHECK scaleb32 wide range derived as [-278, +277] = 556 exponents (EX's BELIEVED figure) ok (-278, 277, 556)
   scaleb64 wide range derived as [-2099, +2098] = 4198 exponents (same argument: emax 1023, smallest subnormal 2^-1074)

CHECK class64 over 2^64 on one quad is about 6,600 years (the lead's COMPUTED)     ok (6584 y)
CHECK rem32 over 2^64 pairs on one quad is about 320,000 years (the lead's COMPUTED) ok (317491 y)
CHECK div64 and rem64 over 2^128 pairs: 10^24 .. 10^26 years on one quad (the lead's COMPUTED) ok (1.75e+24, 4.41e+25 y)
CHECK 35 items run on the tile and 33 are host code                                ok (35, 33)

