== TABLE 3. what the 2026-10-16..19 run covered of each large space, and the defect share it could see
   count = the run's total in the item's own unit (all images), from the rates file; fraction = count / space.
   floor95 = 3 / count: the smallest share of the SAMPLED distribution a defect can occupy and still be hit
   with probability 0.95 by that many independent draws (1 - exp(-3) = 0.95). 'W weekends' means W runs of
   this size with INDEPENDENT samples; with today's seeds a rerun repeats the first (see seed_audit.py).
   For the two 2^32 spaces the run drew MORE than the space; the share of distinct points a uniform
   sampler would have hit is 1 - exp(-fraction) (the banded sampler is not uniform, so this is an upper bound).
   item (rne or only) runs        count, one run    fraction distinct if uniform  floor95 1w floor95 13w floor95 52w
